+# clarify
+
+## Goal
+Make CLI satisfy:
+- (1) `python3 cli.py --version` prints the contents of VERSION
+- (2) `python3 cli.py add 2 3 --json` prints {"result": 5.0}
+
+## Current state
+- VERSION contains `0.3.1`
+- cli.py uses argparse; only has `add` subcommand, no global/version flag, no `--json` for add
+- calc.add exists
+
+## Assumptions (where human answer needed)
+- Treat `--version` as global flag (like standard CLI); print raw VERSION contents (likely with newline/whitespace preserved as-is)
+- For `--json`, print JSON exactly as specified: `{"result": 5.0}` (float 5.0). Use `json.dumps` is fine.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+- `python3 cli.py --version` outputs `0.3.1\n` (contents of VERSION)
+- `python3 cli.py add 2 3 --json` outputs `{"result": 5.0}\n` (exact form matching requirement)
+
+## Out of scope
+- Changing calc logic
+- Other commands/flags
+- Merge to main
